  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1027 PM CDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nAn upper trough axis will slowly track across the area overnight \nThursday into Friday. All models generally concur for rain \npersisting throughout the entire day, with the heaviest rain \nlooking to occur during the midday hours. Cooler temperatures will\naccompany the dreary day, with highs only in the low-to-mid 60s. \nRain will gradually taper off late Friday into Saturday. \nConfidence decreases slightly thereafter. A trailing shortwave may\nbring additional rain chances on Saturday with the ECMWF much \nmore aggressive than the GFS, although ensembles are tending to \nfavor more in the way of scattered showers which makes a bit more \nsense as the wave is generally weak and much of the moisture will \nhave moved through on Friday. In any case, total rainfall around \n1.5-2\" is currently expected, with locally higher amounts \npossible particularly across the southern South Plains. Stay \ntuned for further updates. A weak ridge gives a reprieve on Sunday\nmorning before another system moves in later Sunday into Monday.",
